{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"According to the Mean Value Theorem, there exists a number $c$ in the open interval $2\u003cx\u003c10$ such that $g'(c)$ is equal to the average rate of change of $g$ over the interval:\n\n$g'(c)=\\dfrac{g(10)-g(2)}{(10)-(2)}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"First, let's find that average rate of change:\n\n$\\dfrac{g(10)-g(2)}{(10)-(2)}=\\dfrac{4-0}{8}=\\blueD{\\dfrac{1}{2}}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Now, let's differentiate $g$ and find the $x$-value for which $g'(x)=\\blueD{\\dfrac{1}{2}}$.\n\n$g'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-4}}$ [[☃ explanation 1]]\n\nThe solution of $g'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ is $x=4$.  [[☃ explanation 2]]\n\n$x=4$ is indeed within the interval $2\u003cx\u003c10$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\ng'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\sqrt{2x-4}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(2x-4)^{\\large\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2}(2x-4)^{\\large -\\frac{1}{2}}\\dfrac{d}{dx}(2x-4)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{2x-4}}(2)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-4}}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}},"explanation 2":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\ng'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-4}}\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\\sqrt{2x-4}\u0026=2\n\\\\\\\\\n(\\sqrt{2x-4})^2\u0026=(2)^2\n\\\\\\\\\n2x-4\u0026=4\n\\\\\\\\\n2x\u0026=8\n\\\\\\\\\nx\u0026=4\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $c=4$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $g(x)=\\sqrt{2x-4}$ and let $c$ be the number that satisfies the Mean Value Theorem for $g$ on the interval $2\\leq x\\leq10$.\n\n**What is $c$ ?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$2.25$","correct":false},{"content":"$3.75$","correct":false},{"content":"$4$","correct":true,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$6$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
